<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="git-addon-git-staging-view-interface">
  <title>Git Staging View</title>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>Git Staging view</indexterm></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body>
    <p id="p_pbt_wn5_nsb">The <uicontrol>Git Staging</uicontrol> view is the main interface for
      reviewing changes, staging files, writing commit messages, committing, pushing, and pulling. </p>
    <p>To open the <uicontrol>Git Staging</uicontrol> view, go to either:</p>
    <ul id="ul_git_staging_view_access">
      <li id="li_git_staging_view_access_window"><menucascade>
          <uicontrol>Window</uicontrol>
          <uicontrol>Show View</uicontrol>
          <uicontrol>Git Staging</uicontrol>
        </menucascade></li>
      <li id="li_git_staging_view_access_tools"><menucascade>
          <uicontrol>Tools</uicontrol>
          <uicontrol>Git Client</uicontrol>
        </menucascade></li>
    </ul>
    <p><fig id="fig_tlr_p45_nsb">
        <title>Git Staging View</title>
        <image href="../img/git-addon/staging/staging_view.png" placement="inline"
          id="image_m3r_f5k_gjc"/>
      </fig>
    </p>
    <section id="section_git_staging_view_toolbar"><title>Git Staging Toolbar </title><p
        id="p_git_staging_toolbar_intro">The toolbar contains the main repository-level actions.
        Most of these actions are also available in the top-level <uicontrol>Git</uicontrol> menu.
        For a full list of toolbar actions, see <xref
          href="git-addon-actions-git-staging.dita#git-addon-actions-git-staging"/>.</p><p>On the
          <uicontrol
          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs0-git-staging-view"/>
        toolbar, <uicontrol
          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs1-git-staging-push"/>,
          <uicontrol
          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs2-git-staging-pull"/>, or
            <uicontrol><image href="../img/Stash18.png" id="image_qp1_1mp_pjc"/>Stash</uicontrol>
        changes to perform repository control. Select
          <?oxy_comment_start author="adrian_lapadat" timestamp="20260617T024340+0300" comment="fix ui casing difference this is outrageous haha
"?><uicontrol
          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs4-git-staging-open-history"/>
        or <uicontrol
          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs5-git-staging-open-branch-manager"
        /><?oxy_comment_end?> to view the repository history and manage branches. </p></section>
    <section id="section_git_staging_file_areas">
      <title>Staging Controls</title><p id="p_git_staging_file_areas_intro">Use the staging controls
        to decide which files belong in a commit. </p><p id="p_git_staging_file_context_menu_intro"
        >Right-click a file in either file area to open a context menu with actions for reviewing,
        staging, resolving conflicts, discarding changes, and viewing file history or blame
        information.</p><p><ul>
          <li id="li_rcg_nr5_nsb"><uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> area - Lists changed files
            that are not yet staged.</li>
          <li id="li_tmw_vr5_nsb"><uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol> area - Lists files that are
            ready to be committed.</li>
        </ul></p><p><fig id="fig_git_staging_context_menu">
          <title>Git Staging File Context Menu</title>
          <image href="../img/git-addon/staging/staging_context_menu.png" placement="inline"
            id="image_git_staging_context_menu"/>
        </fig></p><p id="p_git_staging_stage_controls_intro">The controls between the two file areas
        move files between <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> and <uicontrol>Staged
          files</uicontrol>. For a full list, see <xref
          href="git-addon-actions-git-staging.dita#git-addon-actions-git-staging/section_git_staging_stage_controls"
        />.</p></section>
    <section id="section_h5v_bbq_pjc"><title>Staging File Areas</title><p/></section>
    <section id="section_git_staging_file_area_actions"><title>File Area Actions</title><p>These
        actions are available in the context menu of the <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> and
          <uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol> areas. See <xref
          href="git-addon-git-staging-view-interface.dita#git-addon-git-staging-view-interface/section_git_staging_file_areas"
        />.</p><p><table frame="all" rowsep="1" colsep="1" id="table_git_staging_file_area_actions">
          <title>Git Staging file area actions</title>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <colspec colname="c1" colwidth="2*"/>
            <colspec colname="c2" colwidth="5*"/>
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry>Action</entry>
                <entry>Description</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_open_in_compare_editor"
                      ><uicontrol>Open in Compare Editor</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Opens a comparison for the selected changed file so you can review the exact
                  edits before staging or committing it. Also triggered by double-clicking a file in
                  the <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> area.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_open"
                      ><uicontrol>Open</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Opens the selected file, folder, or submodule.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_stage"
                      ><uicontrol>Stage</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Moves the selected unstaged resource to the <uicontrol>Staged
                    files</uicontrol> area.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_discard"
                      ><uicontrol>Discard</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Discards a selected file's unstaged changes and replaces them with the last
                  committed version. Does not discard staged changes.</entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table></p></section>
    <section id="section_git_staging_commit_area"><title>Commit Message Area</title><p
        id="p_git_staging_commit_area_intro">Use the <uicontrol>Commit message</uicontrol> area to
        write the message for the staged changes. For the commit workflow, see <xref
          href="git-addon-committing.dita#git-addon-committing"/>. For a full list of commit area
        actions, see <xref
          href="git-addon-actions-git-staging.dita#git-addon-actions-git-staging/section_git_staging_commit_area_actions"
        />.</p><p><fig id="fig_git_staging_commit_panel">
          <title>Git Staging Commit Message Area</title>
          <image href="../img/git-addon/staging/commit_panel.png" placement="inline"
            id="image_git_staging_commit_panel"/>
        </fig>
      </p>
    </section>
    <section id="section_git_staging_ellipsis_menu"><title>Ellipsis Menu</title><p
        id="p_git_staging_ellipsis_intro">The <uicontrol><image href="../img/Ellipsis18.png"
          />Ellipsis</uicontrol> menu in the toolbar provides access to repository setup,
        synchronization, configuration, and credential actions. For a full list, see <xref
          href="git-addon-actions-shared.dita#git-addon-actions-shared"/> and <xref
          href="git-addon-git-menu.dita#git-addon-git-menu"/>.</p><p><fig
          id="fig_git_staging_actions_menu">
          <title>Git Staging Ellipsis Menu</title>
          <image href="../img/git-addon/staging/staging_actions_menu.png" placement="inline"
            id="image_git_staging_actions_menu"/>
        </fig></p>
    </section>
  </body>
</topic>
